CHAPTER II — GAME MODES
This chapter defines every playable mode in Obsidian Protocol, including traditional RTS modes, autonomous warfare modes, VR cockpit combat, VR operator mode, and modded/custom scenarios.
Each mode is designed to support the game’s core pillars: intent‑based commanding, autonomous squads, emergent battlefields, and cinematic warfare.

2.1 Skirmish Mode
Skirmish is the primary gameplay mode — fast, replayable, endlessly variable.

Purpose
Provide a complete autonomous RTS experience with:

Base building

Resource economy

Autonomous squads

Command units

Experimental units

Dynamic battlefields

Full tech trees

Features
Procedural or handcrafted maps

Fog‑of‑war with elevation, weather, and visibility cones

Autonomous squad behavior (flanking, breaching, suppressing)

Intent‑based commanding

Full faction tech trees

Experimental unit unlocks

Victory conditions (VP, elimination, objectives)

Skirmish Variants
Standard Skirmish — classic RTS structure

Autonomy Mode — squads act with minimal player input

Hardcore Mode — limited command tokens, harsher logistics

No‑Base Mode — pure unit‑vs‑unit tactical engagements

Endless Mode — waves of autonomous enemies

2.2 Campaign Mode
A structured narrative experience built around the Warden Program and the rise of autonomous warfare.

Structure
Story missions with scripted and emergent events

Branching paths based on player decisions

Persistent squads that gain veterancy

Command unit progression

Experimental unit unlock arcs

VR missions integrated into campaign flow

Campaign Elements
Narrative Briefings — strategic context and mission goals

Dynamic Objectives — change based on battlefield conditions

Persistent Losses — destroyed squads remain dead

Logistics Management — supply lines, repair, power grid

Commander Upgrades — unlock new intents, abilities, and bonuses

2.3 Sandbox Mode
A freeform environment for experimentation, testing, and creative play.

Purpose
Let players:

Spawn any unit

Modify stats

Test autonomous behaviors

Simulate large battles

Experiment with command units

Try experimental units without cost

Practice VR dogfights or operator mode

Tools Available
Unit Spawner

Building Spawner

Environmental Controls (weather, time of day, hazards)

AI Personality Editor

Intent Debugger

Autonomy Toggle

VR Mode Access

Sandbox mode is essential for modders, testers, and players who want to explore the game’s systems.

2.4 VR Operator Mode
A hybrid RTS‑VR mode where the player becomes a tactical operator inside the battlefield.

Purpose
Provide immersive, first‑person tactical control without replacing RTS gameplay.

Capabilities
Drone‑jumping — inhabit any drone or sensor unit

Manual recon — sweep areas, tag enemies, mark hazards

Manual strike designation — laser‑mark targets for artillery or airstrikes

Sensor control — adjust LIDAR, thermal, night vision

Operator abilities — EMP bursts, signal jamming, uplink boosts

Tactical overlays — see squad intents, suppression zones, visibility cones

Gameplay Loop
Player issues high‑level RTS intents

Player jumps into VR to support squads

Player returns to RTS view to manage strategy

VR Operator Mode is optional but deeply integrated.

2.5 VR Dogfight Mode
Full cockpit‑level air combat inside the RTS.

Purpose
Let players directly pilot air units in first‑person VR while the RTS battle continues autonomously.

Supported Units
Any air unit with:

Cockpit

Sensor suite

Weapons

Maneuvering capability

Examples: Warden, Beacon, Iris, Nightguard, Overseer, Vector, Watchtower.

Dogfight Mechanics
Full 6‑DOF flight

Altitude bands

Energy management

Afterburners

G‑force simulation

VR HUD (radar, thermal, LIDAR, missile lock indicators)

Damage feedback (cockpit shake, alarms, smoke)

Manual weapon control (guns, missiles, bombs)

Integration With RTS
RTS squads continue fighting autonomously

Player can exit cockpit at any time

Air unit returns to autonomous behavior when player leaves

VR dogfights can influence RTS outcomes (destroy AA, scout, strike targets)

This mode is optional but adds cinematic depth and skill expression.

